flowchart TB
    accTitle: The jobs of a pull request
    accDescr: Each job of a push waits for a runner of its own, and the account runs about 20 jobs at once. So the quick checks share their jobs: lint runs every linter, the title job checks the title and the entry in the changelog, codeql analyzes every language under the category of its alerts, and home-assistant runs HACS and hassfest. Each step runs also when one before it failed, and the PR coach explains each check of a job that failed.

    push["A push to a pull request"]
    lint["lint<br>workflows · licenses · Markdown<br>issue assistant · sign-off · prose"]
    title["conventional title<br>title · entry in the changelog"]
    codeql["codeql<br>every language, one after the other<br>each under /language:name"]
    ha["home-assistant<br>HACS · hassfest"]
    coach["PR coach<br>explains each check that failed"]

    push --> lint
    push --> title
    push --> codeql
    push -- "Home Assistant" --> ha
    lint --> coach
    title --> coach
    codeql --> coach
    ha --> coach

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class push person
    class lint,title,codeql,ha bot
    class coach done
